      "content": "1. Fade to Black (FTB): This is a simple and effective way of transitioning from one scene to another, where the camera slowly fades out until it's completely black before cutting to the next shot. It can be used for both long and short transitions.\n2. Crossfade (XF): A crossfade involves gradually blending two shots together so that they merge seamlessly into each other. The effect creates an illusion of continuity without any abrupt cuts or jarring changes in tone.\n3. Wipe Trans",
